<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f4f1e9] text-slate-950">
  <header id="ai-exploration-hero" class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem] lg:items-end">
      <div class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
          AI for topic exploration
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-5 font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl">
          Use AI to open a question—not close it.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
          AI can open a topic quickly. It is useful for finding questions and comparing views, but it still cannot tell you which answer deserves your confidence.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            id="ai-exploration-start-link"
            href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-slate-800"
          >
            Explore a question <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" />
          </a>
          <a
            href="/intro/how"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-500 px-1 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 transition hover:border-teal-700 hover:text-teal-800"
          >
            Read the guide <.icon name="hero-arrow-up-right" class="h-4 w-4" />
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="border-t border-slate-400 pt-4">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-teal-800">
          A useful role
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
          Let AI suggest possibilities. Keep the work of judging, choosing, and remembering for people.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <section id="ai-exploration-benefits" aria-labelledby="ai-exploration-benefits-heading">
      <div class="grid gap-5 border-b border-slate-400 pb-5 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] sm:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
            Where AI helps
          </p>
          <h2
            id="ai-exploration-benefits-heading"
            class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
          >
            A faster way into a difficult topic.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
          The first answer is a starting point. The value comes from the questions and paths it helps you find next.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-7 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-7 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article id="ai-benefit-map" class="border-t-2 border-sky-500 pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <.icon name="hero-map" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-sky-700" />
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Map the topic quickly</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Find key ideas, useful definitions, examples, and questions before choosing where to spend more time.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="ai-benefit-start" class="border-t-2 border-rose-500 pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <.icon name="hero-chat-bubble-left-right" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-rose-700" />
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Ask before you know the right words</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Start in plain language, even if the question feels basic or awkward to raise, then follow any unfamiliar word, passage, person, book, or idea.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="ai-benefit-views" class="border-t-2 border-violet-500 pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <.icon name="hero-arrows-right-left" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-violet-700" />
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">See more than one side</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Ask for dissenting and less familiar interpretations, then compare their evidence rather than simply counting viewpoints.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="ai-benefit-level" class="border-t-2 border-emerald-500 pt-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <.icon name="hero-adjustments-horizontal" class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-emerald-700" />
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Match the explanation to the reader</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Change the language and depth for a beginner, student, university reader, or expert.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div
        id="ai-benefit-evidence"
        class="mt-8 grid gap-4 border border-stone-300 border-l-4 border-l-sky-600 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(15rem,0.65fr)_minmax(0,1.35fr)] lg:items-center"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <.icon name="hero-document-magnifying-glass" class="h-6 w-6 shrink-0 text-sky-700" />
          <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">
            Find the information behind the claim.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
          RationalGrid asks AI to ground material claims in the source that best fits them: primary sources, original research, official records, or strong scholarly reviews. It also asks for documented fact, interpretation, and speculation to be kept distinct.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="ai-exploration-chat-comparison"
      class="mt-14 border-y border-stone-300 py-10"
      aria-labelledby="ai-exploration-chat-comparison-heading"
    >
      <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
            Chat or grid?
          </p>
          <h2
            id="ai-exploration-chat-comparison-heading"
            class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
          >
            Why not just use ChatGPT or Claude?
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
          You can—and sometimes should. A chat assistant is often the simpler tool for a quick answer, a draft, or a short conversation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-7 overflow-x-auto border border-stone-300 bg-white">
        <table id="ai-chat-feature-table" class="w-full min-w-[48rem] border-collapse text-left">
          <caption class="sr-only">
            A comparison of ChatGPT or Claude with RationalGrid for topic exploration
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-300">
              <th
                scope="col"
                class="w-[24%] bg-stone-100 px-5 py-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-slate-600"
              >
                What you need
              </th>
              <th id="ai-chat-assistants" scope="col" class="w-[34%] bg-stone-100 px-5 py-4">
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800">
                  <.icon name="hero-chat-bubble-left-right" class="h-5 w-5 text-sky-700" />
                  ChatGPT or Claude
                </span>
              </th>
              <th
                id="ai-rationalgrid-branches"
                scope="col"
                class="w-[42%] bg-teal-950 px-5 py-4 text-white"
              >
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold">
                  <.icon name="hero-share" class="h-5 w-5 text-teal-300" /> RationalGrid
                </span>
                <span class="mt-1 block text-xs font-medium text-teal-200">
                  Built for exploration that lasts
                </span>
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-300 text-sm leading-6">
            <%= for {feature, chat, grid} <- [
              {"Get a quick answer", "Excellent for a fast answer, draft, or summary.", "Useful, but not the main reason to choose a grid."},
              {"Follow several paths", "Open more chats or keep adding to one long thread.", "Branch from any idea and explore each path without losing the others."},
              {"See how ideas connect", "The work mainly stays in conversations and documents.", "A visual map keeps the question, answers, evidence, and links in view."},
              {"Ground claims in sources", "You can ask for sources, though a fluent answer can still blur evidence and interpretation.", "Prompts ask for primary sources, original research, official records, or strong reviews that fit the claim."},
              {"Bring ideas together", "Ask for a comparison or synthesis in another prompt.", "Select any two nodes and create a synthesis that keeps both paths attached."},
              {"Return and remember", "Search for and reread earlier conversations.", "Star nodes, save highlights, and return to the exact point that mattered."},
              {"Share a precise idea", "Share a conversation, project, or finished artifact.", "Share the whole grid, one node, or an exact highlighted passage by URL."},
              {"Guide an audience", "Draft an outline or presentation content.", "Choose nodes, order them as slides, and share a guided path through the live grid."},
              {"Explore with other people", "Collaboration depends on the chat product and workspace.", "Edit together, see what other people questioned or chose to emphasise, follow updates, and track each contribution."},
              {"Learn from public work", "A shared chat mainly shows one conversation.", "Public grids can reveal unfamiliar ideas and other people's questions; question or extend any part."}
            ] do %>
              <tr>
                <th
                  scope="row"
                  class="bg-[#f8f6f0] px-5 py-4 align-top font-semibold text-slate-900"
                >
                  {feature}
                </th>
                <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top text-slate-600">{chat}</td>
                <td class="bg-teal-50 px-5 py-4 align-top font-medium text-slate-800">
                  <span class="flex gap-2.5">
                    <.icon name="hero-check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal-700" />
                    <span>{grid}</span>
                  </span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div
        id="ai-chat-comparison-takeaway"
        class="mt-6 flex gap-3 border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-4"
      >
        <.icon
          name="hero-arrow-path-rounded-square"
          class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal-700"
        />
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-slate-800">
          Use chat when the answer is the output. Use a grid when the path matters too—so you can return to it, check it, and build on it with other people.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="ai-exploration-objections"
      class="mt-14 border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-6 text-white sm:p-8"
      aria-labelledby="ai-exploration-objections-heading"
    >
      <div class="grid gap-5 border-b border-slate-700 pb-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber-300">
            Common objections
          </p>
          <h2
            id="ai-exploration-objections-heading"
            class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
          >
            The concerns are real.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">
          RationalGrid does not make AI trustworthy. It gives you a place to question it, keep sources close, and show your own work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="divide-y divide-slate-700">
        <%= for {number, slug, title, response, tone} <- [
          {"01", "wrong", "It can be wrong with confidence.", "Treat every answer as a lead, not a fact. Check important claims against reliable sources before you rely on them.", "text-rose-300"},
          {"02", "passive", "It can make learning passive.", "Do not ask AI to think for you. Choose the questions, add your own notes, and return to important ideas without asking AI again.", "text-amber-300"},
          {"03", "bias", "It can repeat an echo chamber.", "AI reflects patterns in its training data and the way a question is framed. Ask which voices and interpretations are missing, then compare the evidence. Another view is not automatically an equally sound one.", "text-violet-300"},
          {"04", "uncertainty", "Clear writing can hide uncertainty.", "Split an answer into claims you can check. Keep doubts, exceptions, and sources visible instead of treating fluent writing as proof.", "text-sky-300"},
          {"05", "ownership", "It can blur who did the work.", "Use AI as a tutor or research partner, not a hidden author. Add your own reasoning, show contributions, and follow the rules of your school or workplace.", "text-emerald-300"},
          {"06", "costs", "It has privacy and wider costs.", "Do not enter private or confidential information. AI also uses energy and money, so use it when it adds real value rather than for every step.", "text-orange-300"}
        ] do %>
          <article
            id={"ai-objection-#{slug}"}
            class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[2.5rem_17rem_1fr] sm:items-baseline lg:grid-cols-[2.5rem_20rem_1fr]"
          >
            <p class={["font-mono text-xs font-bold", tone]}>{number}</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-white">{title}</h3>
            <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{response}</p>
          </article>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <p class="border-t border-slate-700 pt-5 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-400">
        These habits reduce risk; they do not remove it. Important decisions still need reliable evidence and human judgement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      id="ai-exploration-roles"
      class="mt-14"
      aria-labelledby="ai-exploration-roles-heading"
    >
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
          A better division of work
        </p>
        <h2
          id="ai-exploration-roles-heading"
          class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Keep people in charge of the meaning.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-7 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-stone-300 bg-stone-300 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article id="ai-role-ai" class="bg-white p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-sky-700">AI SUGGESTS</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">Possibilities</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Definitions, examples, questions, comparisons, and new directions to examine.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article id="ai-role-person" class="bg-white p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-violet-700">YOU DECIDE</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">What matters</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Which question to follow, which evidence to trust, and what you finally think.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article id="ai-role-grid" class="bg-white p-6">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-emerald-700">THE GRID KEEPS</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">The path</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Questions, sources, highlights, notes, and the links between them.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border border-stone-300 border-l-4 border-l-teal-700 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
        Try the approach
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Start with a question you genuinely care about.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Let AI open a few paths. Then choose what to check, keep, and develop yourself.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-slate-800"
        >
          <.icon name="hero-plus" class="h-4 w-4" /> Start a grid
        </a>
        <a
          href="/about"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-stone-300 bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-teal-800 transition hover:border-teal-700"
        >
          <.icon name="hero-information-circle" class="h-4 w-4" /> About RationalGrid
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>
